that is closest to the ocean. On the other hand the leeward is the farthest from shore and is drier but still gets rain.

passage 3:The Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea. The Windward Islands are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. They’re called the Windward Islands because they’re exposed to the wind (“windward”) of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). Martinique.

